# Python Imports

Always use absolute imports rooted at `src/`. Never use relative imports.

```python
# ❌ BAD — relative imports
from .models import Document
from ..shared.config import Settings

# ✅ GOOD — absolute imports from src root
from shared.models import Document
from shared.config import Settings
from backend.domain.models import User
from data_pipeline.pipeline import DataPipeline
from data_pipeline.steps import FileDocumentLoader
```

The `src/` directory is on `PYTHONPATH` (configured in `pyproject.toml` via `[tool.ruff] src = ["src"]`). All imports should reference packages directly: `shared`, `backend`, `data_pipeline`.
